      "writtenOn": "2026-07-06T06:38:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand this CL is swapping the FFI bindings so this is just preserving the existing state, but in a similar vein to my reviews on the crate introducing the types, I\u0027m concerned about the ambiguity with terminology that the API shape is introducing.\n\nThis is a \"Label\" just as there is a \"Label\" in Starlark land, but it is actually a GN \"Label\" which has the toolchain, and conceptual translations between GN-shaped data and Starlark-shaped data are being pushed right into the FFI layer.\n\nSo this API says a GN \"Label\" in Rust land gets to have a `.package` which is a Bazel/Starlark-shaped declaration. Likewise `as_ref` drops the toolchain.\n\nIn the pre-diff version I would\u0027ve been understanding that this conceptual translation is pushed into FFI so that consumers don\u0027t worry about `unsafe`, but that\u0027s now no longer the case.\n\nThere\u0027s no more `unsafe`s here, so why is conceptual translation of GN concepts into Bazel/Starlark concepts happening at the FFI layer?\n\nAgain, this is a comment on what\u0027s already landed and I won\u0027t block submit on the CL being a migration of FFI methods itself.",
      "revId": "95322ed322bb367f42d354883f74c52f9adf51f6",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
